{"seq":1,"mint":"C14","verb":"claim","status":"ok","model":"openai/gpt-5.6-luna","approach":"split","literals":true,"findings":[{"kind":"contradicts","clause":"An absolute label is structural","clause_quoted":true,"facts":["F6","F21"],"quoted_from":"output","evidence":"let (shown, label) = match lines {\n        None => (contents.clone(), path.to_string()),","why":"The label is taken directly from the supplied path rather than structurally normalized to an absolute path; a relative input can therefore yield a relative label.","quoted":true},{"kind":"contradicts","clause":"No amount of author care can produce a relative label over MCP.","clause_quoted":true,"facts":[],"why":"The server accepts relative path inputs by resolving them against its working directory, while the look label preserves the supplied spelling. Thus an author can produce a relative label over the server.","quoted":false,"rejected_span":"//! Every path a tool takes (`look`'s `path`, `render`'s `out`,\n//! `check`/`brief`/`record`'s memo) is resolved against **this server's**\n//! working directory, which is wherever the client happened to start it —\n//! not the caller's, and not anything the caller can see or set. A\n//! relative path therefore resolves somewhere the caller cannot predict.\n\nlet (shown, label) = match lines {\n        None => (contents.clone(), path.to_string()),"}],"at":1790111824,"cost":0.018840684,"elapsed_ms":85373,"attempts":5,"not_verbatim":0,"literals_refuted":0,"not_a_quantity":0,"kind_off_verb":0,"refuted":0,"typed_versions":["jev-1.13.0"],"gate_calls":1,"typed_classify_calls":1,"typed_literal_calls":1}
